The owner's buttons are the model's own words and nothing checked them:
„დიახ, სთხოვენ გაცნობა" / „არა, დეველოდოთ ლევანის პასუხს" after an answer
card (conv 43319, 43327), and today „ვცალობ", „არსად არ ვდადი". The
helper's question already passes an editor (D711).

Misho's yes, 8 Oct ~16:55 UTC, recorded with the exact brief as §105:
before a reply with buttons is stored, the model-written buttons (never
the server's approve / change / other / later labels) go to the same
editor model with that brief; a usable rewrite (same count, non-empty, at
most 40 characters, no repeats) replaces them, anything else keeps them
as written.

DONE WHEN: on a fresh trio after one helper answers, the owner's buttons
under the answer card are correct Georgian, e.g. „კი, სთხოვე გაცნობა" /
„არა, ჯერ ლევანს დაველოდოთ" / „სხვა, მე დავწერ".

